      "claimId": "C10925-1",
      "statement": "Hillingdon Council has approved a 15% increase on most discretionary fees and charges to raise an estimated £3.3 million.",
      "sourceQuote": "Hillingdon Council's Cabinet has approved a 15% increase on most discretionary fees and charges for the upcoming financial year, aiming to address a significant shortfall in government funding. The proposed increases have the potential to increase the Council's income by an estimated £3.3 million.",
      "sourceDocument": "CABINET Hillingdon, 22 October 2026",
      "sourceDocumentUrl": "https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/g5211/Agenda%20frontsheet%2022nd-Oct-2026%2019.00%20CABINET.pdf?T=0",
      "verified": true
    },
    {
      "claimId": "C10925-2",
      "statement": "The borough faces a £65 million government funding shortfall over the next two years.",
      "sourceQuote": "This shortfall is attributed to the government's revised funding formula, which will result in Hillingdon not receiving £65 million of assessed government funding over the next two years.",
      "sourceDocument": "CABINET Hillingdon, 22 October 2026",
      "sourceDocumentUrl": "https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/g5211/Agenda%20frontsheet%2022nd-Oct-2026%2019.00%20CABINET.pdf?T=0",
      "verified": true
    },
    {
      "claimId": "C10925-3",
      "statement": "Resident parking discounts will be reduced from roughly 40% to 10%, though 30 minutes free parking is preserved.",
      "sourceQuote": "The resident discount will be reduced from approximately 40% to 10%. This change aims to move the cost closer to outer London averages while still providing a discount and retaining free parking entitlements for residents. Crucially, 30 minutes of free parking for residents will be retained",
      "sourceDocument": "CABINET Hillingdon, 22 October 2026",
      "sourceDocumentUrl": "https://modgov.hillingdon.gov.uk/documents/g5211/Agenda%20frontsheet%2022nd-Oct-2026%2019.00%20CABINET.pdf?T=0",
      "verified": true
    }
